<%#
  THE BILL OF MATERIALS' COMPOSER, on its own (2026-11-02, the UX audit's B3/C4/C5). It lived inside
  projects/_bom_lines, which the panel renders only once a line exists, so "+ Add panel → Bill of
  materials" opened a panel with no way to add the first line (C5). Now the panel draws it in its
  head whether or not a line exists, the BOM page draws it under its table, and a refused line
  comes back through Projects::ComposerRefusal as this partial again — open, with the error inside
  it and the typed values in their fields.

  Locals:
    project   — the Maker::Project the form posts against
    items     — [[name, id], …] for the stock select
    suppliers — [[name, id], …] for the supplier select
  Optional (a refusal):
    draft     — the refused Maker::BomLine (unsaved), whose attributes refill the fields
    kind      — the target radio that was chosen ("stock" | "file" | "text")
    file_name — the chosen file's name, the chooser's label
    error     — the sentence the door refused with
    open      — render it open

  EVERY FIELD STATES ITS VALUE. A scoped `form_with url:` reads `@bom_line` for a field that names
  none (CLAUDE.md §14d's form-scope lesson, and the fallback it hides), so nothing here is left to
  the builder's guess.

  scope: :bom_line — WITHOUT it, a model-less form_with(url:) has a blank object_name, and
  fields_for-style bracketing breaks (CLAUDE.md §14d, the trap projects/_tasks.html.erb's own
  comment records). Every field below is a plain f.* call for exactly that reason.
%>
<% draft = local_assigns[:draft] %>
<% kind = local_assigns[:kind] %>
<% error = local_assigns[:error] %>
<details class="composer bom-add" id="bom-composer" <%= "open" if local_assigns[:open] %>>
  <summary class="btn small" aria-label="Add a line to the bill of materials">Add…</summary>
  <%= form_with url: project_bom_lines_path(project), scope: :bom_line, method: :post, class: "bom-add-form" do |f| %>
    <% if error.present? %><div class="form-errors flash-alert composer-error" role="alert"><%= error %></div><% end %>
    <div class="composer-fields">
      <label class="field">
        <span>Reference</span>
        <%= f.text_field :reference, value: draft&.reference %>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Quantity</span>
        <%= f.number_field :quantity, step: "any", value: draft ? draft.read_attribute_before_type_cast(:quantity) : 1 %>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Unit</span>
        <%= f.select :unit, Maker::BomLine::UNITS, selected: draft&.read_attribute(:unit) %>
      </label>
    </div>

    <%# EXACTLY ONE TARGET, CHOSEN BY THE RADIO: Projects::BomLinesController#create is what
        actually enforces this (it drops the other two inputs server-side before the line is
        built), so a client that fills more than one field and picks the "wrong" radio still gets
        the target it chose, never a validation error about a field it never meant to set. EACH
        CONTROL CARRIES ITS OWN NAME (the UX audit's §I): a label names only its first control, the
        radio, so the select, the chooser and the text field say what they are themselves. %>
    <fieldset class="bom-target">
      <legend>Target</legend>
      <label>
        <%= f.radio_button :target_kind, "stock", checked: kind == "stock" %>
        <span>Stock</span>
        <%= f.select :inventory_item_id, items, { include_blank: true, selected: draft&.inventory_item_id },
                     { "aria-label": "Stock item" } %>
      </label>
      <label>
        <%= f.radio_button :target_kind, "file", checked: kind == "file" %>
        <span>File</span>
        <%= render "shared/folder_field", name: "bom_line[node_id]",
                   children_url: library_children_path, create_url: library_folders_path,
                   mode: "file", root_label: "Choose a file…", value: draft&.node_id,
                   label: local_assigns[:file_name].presence || "Choose a file…" %>
      </label>
      <label>
        <%= f.radio_button :target_kind, "text", checked: kind == "text" %>
        <span>Part name</span>
        <%= f.text_field :part_name, value: draft&.part_name, placeholder: "e.g. 22 AWG wire", "aria-label": "Part name" %>
      </label>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="composer-fields">
      <label class="field">
        <span>Supplier</span>
        <%= f.select :supplier_id, suppliers, include_blank: true, selected: draft&.supplier_id %>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Notes</span>
        <%= f.text_field :notes, value: draft&.notes %>
      </label>
    </div>

    <%# A QUIET `.btn`: the hub's one accent is the top bar's Upload (design-system.md rule 13), and
        this submit was a second one the moment the composer opened (the UX audit's C4). %>
    <%= f.submit "Add line", class: "btn small" %>
  <% end %>
</details>
